moment needs, not all the same length), that work on their own without
context: provocative, funny, quotable, a strong claim or a sharp one-liner.
Skip pre-show and housekeeping, prefer a mix of speakers, start on the setup
and end right after the punchline. Leave out anything whose point rests on a
slur. A person will choose which of them get cut, so make each one clearly
different from the others.
{brief}
Answer one clip per line, exactly:
N | START H:MM:SS | END H:MM:SS | speaker | hook title (max 6 words) | until LASTWORD | what is said and why it works, one sentence
START is the stamp of the first sentence, END the stamp of the last sentence
included, LASTWORD the last word of that sentence (it pins the cut when two
sentences share a stamp).

{transcript}"""


def prompt(a):
    meta = os.path.join(a.dir, 'meta.tsv')
    title = open(meta).read().split('\t')[0] if os.path.exists(meta) else 'a recording'
    brief = a.brief or ''
    if a.brief_file:
        brief = open(a.brief_file).read().strip()
    if brief:
        brief = ('\nWhat the person is looking for, which matters more than the general\n'
                 'advice above:\n' + brief.strip() + '\n')
    print(PROMPT.format(title=title, n=a.n, lo=a.min, hi=a.max, brief=brief,
                        transcript=open(os.path.join(a.dir, 'transcript-ts.txt')).read()))


